symbols.remarks:
`sizes` attribute for a masonry image (`?image` srcset): the column width per breakpoint. Breakpoints are container
widths; `sizes` media queries are viewport widths, so the container is described relative to the viewport:
container = `min(100vw − inset, maxWidth)` (`inset`: px of the viewport outside the grid — page padding, a sidebar;
`maxWidth`: the grid's `maxWidth`). A breakpoint at container width `min` then starts at viewport `min + inset`;
from viewport `maxWidth + inset` on, every width is a constant. `span` = columns the image covers (number or
container-width map, e.g. a live span's current value).

Interactions outside `element` (React Aria `useInteractOutside`): a pointerdown outside starts
one (`onInteractOutsideStart`), the following click outside completes it (`onInteractOutside`;
click rather than pointerup for Android Chrome). Capture phase. Returns the remove function.

members.doc:
Called after the Group's layout has been changed (pointer: once released). Recommended for persisting layouts;
`meta.isUserInteraction` is true for pointer / keyboard input, `meta.requestedLayout` is the layout before
size-dependent constraints (prefer it when persisting).

symbols.remarks:
Formats a day number (labels: weekday names, day of month, titles). `options` are `Intl.DateTimeFormat` options;
the zone is fixed to UTC (day numbers are wall-clock days), the calendar follows the locale (`-u-ca-…`).
Formatters are cached per locale + options (`i18n/intl-cache`).

Global DOM events and attributes (RAC GlobalDOMAttributes) go to the root element (RAC `Select`);
the parts RAC composes take theirs through `triggerProps` (the `<Button>`), `valueProps`
(`<SelectValue>`), `popoverProps` (`<Popover>`) and `listBoxProps` (`<ListBox>`).
